WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
One of the coolest things in the wind tunnel

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.788
is to see water floating.

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:07.926
Poured from a jug it quickly breaks up into droplets

00:00:07.926 --> 00:00:09.710
the same size&nbsp;as raindrops

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.948
from around 0.5 to 4 millimeters in diameter.

00:00:12.948 --> 00:00:14.694
And standing there

00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:18.406
you can experience&nbsp;what it would be like to fall with raindrops

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.393
They have a low terminal velocity of just 25&nbsp;km/h

00:00:24.393 --> 00:00:27.429
that's what the wind speed was set to for this demonstration

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:33.125
and&nbsp;what you can see is that raindrops aren't shaped like cartoon raindrops

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:39.795
They are closer to&nbsp;spherical but a bit flatter on the bottom where they encounter oncoming air.

00:00:39.795 --> 00:00:41.550
If a raindrop gets&nbsp;
too big,

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.848
it flattens out, caves in in the middle,

00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:46.273
and briefly resembles a little parachute

00:00:46.273 --> 00:00:49.249
before breaking up into smaller droplets

